              "content": "#!/bin/bash\n\n# NOTE: This script's logic appears to dynamically calculate the number of\n# nodes based on the LSB_DJOB_NUMPROC variable, which is not available in Flux.\n# You must explicitly request the number of nodes needed for the job.\n# The following is a placeholder for a single-node job.\n#FLUX --nodes=1\n\n# The original script used 'jsrun' which maps resources based on resource sets.\n# Each resource set got all CPUs and all GPUs. Assuming 4 GPUs per node, this\n# means we want 1 task per node, with access to all resources.\n#FLUX --ntasks-per-node=1\n#FLUX --gpus-per-task=4\n#FLUX --cpus-per-task=0 # Request all CPUs on the node\n\n# NOTE: The LSF directive 'alloc_flags atsdisable' is highly system-specific\n# and has been omitted as there is no standard equivalent in Flux. This could have\n# performance implications if the workload is sensitive to Adaptive-Time Slicing.\n\n# n=$(( ($FLUX_JOB_NUM_TASKS) )) # This would be the Flux equivalent if num_procs were total tasks\n# Assuming 'n' is the number of nodes, as calculated in the original script.\nn=$FLUX_JOB_NNODES\nnumgpus=4\n\necho Num nodes: $numnodes\necho Job id: $FLUX_JOB_ID\n\nmodule load gcc/7.3.1\nmodule load cmake/3.14.5\nmodule load cuda/11.7.0\n\nroot_dir=\"$PWD\"\nexport LD_LIBRARY_PATH=\"$PWD\"\n\nrepeat=5\n\nrun() {\n  local nx=$1;\n  local ny=$2;\n  local ncx=$3;\n  local ncy=$4;\n  local nox=$5;\n  local noy=$6;\n  local tile=$7;\n\n  local oricmd=\" -tsteps 50 -tprune 30 -hl:sched 1024 -ll:gpu ${numgpus} -ll:util 1 -ll:bgwork 2 -ll:csize 150000 -ll:fsize 15000 -ll:zsize 2048 -ll:rsize 512 -ll:gsize 0 -level 5 -dm:replicate 1 -dm:same_address_space -dm:memoize -lg:no_fence_elision -lg:parallel_replay 2 \"\n\n  local logori=$oricmd\" -wrapper -level mapper=debug -logfile wrapper_${nx}_${ny}_${nox}_${noy}_n%.wrapper -lg:prof ${n} -lg:prof_logfile prof_${nx}_${ny}_${nox}_${noy}_n%.gz \"\n  local logcpl=$oricmd\" -wrapper -level mapper=debug -logfile wrapper_${nx}_${ny}_${ncx}_${ncy}_n%.wrapper -lg:prof ${n} -lg:prof_logfile prof_${nx}_${ny}_${ncx}_${ncy}_n%.gz \"\n\n\n  if [[ ! -d ratio_${n}_${nx}_${ny} ]]; then mkdir ratio_${n}_${nx}_${ny}; fi\n  pushd ratio_${n}_${nx}_${ny}\n\n  # 'jsrun' is replaced by 'flux run'. The resource mapping options are handled\n  # by the job-level directives.\n  flux run -n $n \"$root_dir/stencil\"  -nx $(( nx * ${tile} )) -ny $(( ny * ${tile} )) -ntx ${nox} -nty ${noy} $logori\n  flux run -n $n \"$root_dir/stencil\"  -nx $(( nx * ${tile} )) -ny $(( ny * ${tile} )) -ntx ${ncx} -nty ${ncy} $logcpl\n  for (( r=1; r <= ${repeat}; r++)); do\n    echo \"Running ${nx}_${ny}_r${r}\"\n    flux run -n $n \"$root_dir/stencil\"  -nx $(( nx * ${tile} )) -ny $(( ny * ${tile} )) -ntx ${nox} -nty ${noy} $oricmd | tee out_${nx}_${ny}_${nox}_${noy}_r${r}.log\n    flux run -n $n \"$root_dir/stencil\"  -nx $(( nx * ${tile} )) -ny $(( ny * ${tile} )) -ntx ${ncx} -nty ${ncy} $oricmd | tee out_${nx}_${ny}_${ncx}_${ncy}_r${r}.log\n  done\n\n  popd\n}\n\n# 1250 * 1250 * 256 = 10000 * 10000 * 4\n# run nx ny ncx ncy nox noy tile\nrun 1 256 16 8 1 128 7076\nrun 2 128 16 8 1 128 7076\nrun 4 64 16 8 2 64 7076\nrun 8 32 16 8 4 32 7076\nrun 16 16 16 8 8 16 7076\nrun 32 8 16 8 16 8 7076\nrun 64 4 16 8 32 4 7076\nrun 128 2 16 8 64 2 7076\nrun 256 1 16 8 128 1 7076\n"
